A||N||4||87ECO5||Best way to clean white-lettered tires||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||07-13-2000||09:28 PM||||I've got a set of Goodyear Eagle ST white-lettered tires on my coupe right now.  To clean the letters (make them white), I've been using Comet cleaner and a scrub brush.  The letters get nice and white but I'm seeing white "stains" on the black rubber now.<P>Anyway, I've got a new set of white-lettered tires I'm about to put on the car this weekend and I'd like to avoid this same problem with the new rubber.<P>So, I'm looking for suggestions on what to use to clean the white-lettered tires before I dress them.  The proverbial wrench in the works here is that I'm mounting them on newly repainted rims so I can't use a chemical that will harm the rim's painted finish.<P>Suggestions?  TIA ...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||07-13-2000||10:21 PM||||I have Goodyear T/A Radials with the white lettering showing.  I use SuperClean.  It's like 409 and Simple Green but stronger.  I get it at WalMart for about $2 to $3 for a spray bottle.  I get the gallon refill.<P>Spray it on the tires and rims and let it sit for a few minutes.  Then I use a stiff bristle tire brush wetted down with SuperClean.  I scrub the tires with the straight SuperClean and then dip the brush in the bucket full of carwash and water and scrub them again to rinse off the brake dust etc.  Spray them clean with a hose.<P>After I finish washing the car I use tire foam to spruce them up.<P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-13-2000||10:23 PM||||BTW,<P>I also use the SuperClean as an engine degreaser.  Spray it on and let it sit for a few minutes.  Hit the grimy spots with a stiff brush and then hose off.  I have never had any electrical problems after having done this.  The car always starts and runs fine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||07-13-2000||10:44 PM||||Bleche-White by far.  It works absolutely great!  Makes tires look like new!  Doesn't harm paint or aluminum either.  Just use it with a nylon brush.  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||07-14-2000||03:03 PM||||Found some stuff called Mean Green at dollar General. Like Simple Green, but seems to work waaaayyyy better.||||reg||1
